# Default config for nektos/act (https://github.com/nektos/act).
# Lets contributors run our GitHub Actions CI locally without burning
# GitHub-hosted runner minutes. See README.md "Local CI" for usage.

# Map ubuntu-latest to a medium-size catthehacker image. The default `act`
# slim image is ~200MB but lacks build tools (gcc, make, curl, sudo) that
# our cargo + capnproto + apt-get steps need. The `act-latest` medium
# image (~1.5GB) ships those tools and is the de-facto standard for
# CI-parity runs.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest runners are amd64. On Apple Silicon hosts,
# act would otherwise default to arm64 images and silently diverge from
# production behavior (different apt package availability, different
# rustc host triple). Pin to amd64 so local runs match what GitHub will
# actually run. Costs some emulation overhead on M-series Macs.
--container-architecture linux/amd64
